      "reason": "Weighted 91.25. >= 80, selected. Materially new vs AgentLab's 2026-10-27 article, which reported the group had decided not to release the AI-produced material. GitHub API: yang-mills-group/YM created 2026-11-10T16:45:55Z, single commit 'Assemble October Yang-Mills assessment and verification' by Michael R Douglas 2026-11-10T21:09:02Z, pushed 2026-11-11T03:38:25Z (all in window); archive repo OpenAI-YM-20261028 created 2026-11-05 (private prep), Apache-2.0, Lean ~64 MB. Assessment PDF (35 pp, dated Nov 10 2026) read: Wightman QFT constructed as scaling limit of 4D Wilson lattice gauge theory for any simple compact group; no uniqueness of infinite-volume limit, no mass gap, not the full Jaffe-Witten problem. Clean rebuild 9,470 modules ~184 min zero errors; 250,319 declarations, no project axioms/sorryAx; only propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound; Comparator passed Oct 30 and Nov 3 with four controls; 2,453 warnings and code-quality concerns; group says it does not yet fully understand the proof. AgentLab did not rebuild the Lean proof."
